Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Set the default child PATH for the on-device Linux tree

dropbear builds a fixed environment for each session (it does not pass its own
environment through), and PATH comes from DEFAULT_PATH. The upstream default
"/usr/bin:/bin" does not exist on this device, so every applet lookup failed
even though the static BusyBox tree is on disk.

--- a/default_options.h
+++ b/default_options.h
@@ -351,7 +351,7 @@
 #define DEFAULT_IDLE_TIMEOUT 0
 
 /* The default path. This will often get replaced by the shell */
-#define DEFAULT_PATH "/usr/bin:/bin"
+#define DEFAULT_PATH "/data/local/tmp/linux/bin:/system/bin:/system/xbin"
 #define DEFAULT_ROOT_PATH "/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin"
 
 #endif /* DROPBEAR_DEFAULT_OPTIONS_H_ */
